# A candidate that never finishes.
#
# The commonest way an AI-written repair to a hunting script goes wrong is not
# a syntax error - `ruby -c` catches those - it is a loop whose exit condition
# the patch removed. Under Lich that script runs until somebody notices. Under
# containment the wall clock ends it and the result says `timedOut`, with the
# commands it had already tried still in `sent`, which is the part a reviewer
# needs in order to see what it was doing when the clock ran out.

echo 'loop_forever: starting'

fput 'search corpse'

loop do
  # No pause: pausing is recorded and returns at once under the shim, so a
  # sleep here would be measuring the shim rather than the wall clock.
  Time.now
end
